    "description": "onsemi ${mpn}, a ${vdrm} V, 0.8 A RMS sensitive-gate silicon controlled rectifier in TO-92 (K1, G2, A3): gate trigger current 200 uA and voltage 0.8 V at most, holding current 5 mA at most (with 1 kohm gate to cathode), on-state voltage 1.7 V at most at 1.2 A. The model is the thyristor's two-transistor equivalent: it latches on a gate pulse, holds above its holding current and blocks both ways until it breaks over.",
